:: the_betrayal__first_secret [the_betrayal]
<!-- harness:meta
location: cartography_shop
-->

Maren sits on the top step, arms wrapped around her knees. She is nineteen and has been your apprentice for two years. She is better at inking than you were at her age. You have never told her that.

"You can make things real," she says. Not a question.

You could lie. You could tell her the ink bled from a bad batch, that the stove fire made the parchment smoke. She would believe you. She trusts you.

But the river outside is still flowing, and the Guild has already branded your door.

"Yes," you say.

Her eyes are very wide. And then they change. Not fear. Something else. Calculation.

"Teach me," she says.

<<set $apprentice_loyalty to $apprentice_loyalty - 1>>

